<title>UK: UK July bank mortgage lending up 615 mln stg - BBA.</title>
<headline>UK July bank mortgage lending up 615 mln stg - BBA.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-08-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>The British Bankers Association released the following data for net lending for house purchase by financial institutions in July.</p>
<p>(in millions of stg unless otherwise stated)</p>
<p> Month		net lending(s/a)  total gross lending</p>
<p> July		 +615		  2,607</p>
<p> June		 +591		  2,233</p>
<p>NOTES - (s/a) = seasonally adjusted.</p>
<p>The BBA said the data were encouraging. &quot;Taken together with the figures published by the building societies, the likelihood is that seasonally-adjusted net lending by all mortgage providers was a little stronger than June,&quot; said Tim Sweeney, director general of the BBA.</p>
<p>&quot;Overall the industry data point to a continuation of gradual housing market recovery.&quot;</p>
<p>-- Rosemary Bennett +44 171 542 7715</p>
